by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-02T09:13:24Z

I reworked this while preparing it for merge, in a simpler direction than my earlier comments asked for.

The `message_system_attribute_names` option is gone: the transport now always requests `All` system attributes and fills the stamp. Requesting them is the same API call with a marginally larger response, so there is nothing to save by trimming the list. This also dissolves both points from my last review: there is no user-provided list to validate anymore, and no empty default that would hide the feature.

Always sending `MessageSystemAttributeNames` requires async-aws/sqs 2.1, where that request parameter was added, so the constraint is bumped from `^1.0|^2.0` to `^2.1`. SQS-compatible test servers that predate the parameter ignore it and return no attributes, so nothing breaks there; `getSystemAttributes()` just returns an empty array.

I also rebased on current 8.2, resolved the conflicts with the recent `ssl` option and FIFO deduplication changes, and updated the changelog entry to name the new method.

@maxbaldanza the result keeps your stamp extension and tests, with your authorship. Thank you for the feature and for your patience.
